    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0692" n="608" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg608"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3146</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-11T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1325. For Dresel:</p>
                <p>By authority of his Government, Serbian Minister here has requested that American
                    Red Cross include the provisioning of Montenegrin prisoners in enemy countries
                    with the proposed and practically accepted plan of the provisioning of all
                    Serbian prisoners by the Red Cross. Number of prisoners stated to be small.
                    Department <pb facs="0693" n="609" xml:id="pg609"/> understands that such
                    Serbian relief as has been sent you is administered under your supervision by
                    the Serbian Belief Bureau and distributed by Swiss delegates to prisoners under
                    guarantees of enemy Governments that supplies will not be diverted. Is this
                    correct? If so, will Serbian Belief Bureau undertake administration and obtain
                    similar guarantees from enemy Governments for Montenegrin prisoners? Cable
                    fully.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
